{
  "configuration_id": "config_011",
  "reason": "Evidence: The image-only single-profile baseline (config_010) yielded only ~20.8% accuracy, far below the RNA-only baselines, but this was tested with a single profile. For RNA, moving from single-profile to multi-profile was the single largest lever discovered (+13 points, config_004→config_005). It is currently unknown whether the image modality's apparent weakness is due to an inherent lack of signal or simply the single-profile limitation. Question tested: config_011 (image-only, multi-profile, ResNet50, avgpool) directly parallels the RNA multi-profile experiment and isolates whether multi-profile aggregation recovers meaningful image signal. Why this is the best next experiment: The result will determine whether any multimodal fusion experiment is worth pursuing. If image multi-profile remains very weak (~20-30%), it strongly suggests the image modality carries little independent signal and budget should be redirected to RNA-only improvements (e.g., scgpt encoder). If it jumps substantially, it validates the image modality and justifies investing in multimodal fusion configs. This single, clean experiment resolves a major branch of the search tree and avoids committing budget to multimodal configurations whose value is currently unestablished."
}

